==English==

===Etymology===
< {{etyl|la}} {{term|elevatus}}, pp. of {{term|elevare||to raise, lift up}} < {{term|e||out}} + {{term|levare||to make light, to lift}} < {{term|levis||light}}; see [[levity]] and [[lever]].

===Verb===
{{en-verb|elevat|ing}}

# {{transitive}} To [[raise]] (something) to a [[higher]] [[position]]; to [[lift]].
# {{transitive}} To [[promote]] (someone) to a higher [[rank]].
# {{transitive}} To [[ennoble]] or [[honour]]/[[honor]] (someone).
# {{transitive}} To lift someone's [[spirit]]s; to [[elate]].
# {{transitive}} To [[increase]] the [[intensity]] of something, especially that of [[sound]].

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|raise}} [[lift]], [[raise]]
* {{sense|promote}} [[promote]]
* {{sense|ennoble}} [[ennoble]], [[honour]]/[[honor]]
* {{sense|elate}} [[cheer up]], [[elate]]
* {{sense|increase the intensity of}} [[increase]], [[raise]], [[turn up]], [[up]] {{informal}}

====Antonyms====
* {{sense|raise}} [[drop]], [[lower]]
* {{sense|promote}} [[demote]]
* {{sense|elate}} [[depress]], [[sadden]]
* {{sense|increase the intensity of}} [[decrease]], [[diminish]], [[lower]], [[reduce]], [[turn down]]

